    "id": "v2-2-practice-section-slot-5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Sketch $y=\\tan(x)+c$ on Desmos and create a slider for $c$.\nDescribe how the graph changes as $c$ increases.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "As $c$ increases, the graph shifts upwards. The vertical asymptotes do not move.",
      "worked": "Increasing $c$ adds the same amount to every $y$-value, so the graph shifts upwards without changing its shape. The period is still $\\pi$ and the vertical asymptotes stay in the same places.",
